-- Generated by chezmoi. On exe.dev VMs this disables NvChad-shipped plugins the
-- VM profile does not want. Lazy imports spec files in alphabetical module
-- order and `nvchad.plugins` is imported first, so `zz-*` is the last fragment
-- and its `enabled = false` entries win (lazy's meta layer: last fragment wins,
-- and a disabled plugin is removed from the install set entirely, so it is
-- never cloned).
--
-- An `enabled = false` here is the only way to drop a plugin that NvChad's own
-- import declares; the `.chezmoiignore` whitelist only covers this repo's specs.
--
-- Everything else on the VM comes from NvChad's import list, minus:
--   menu   : NvChad's option menu; nothing in nvchad/ui consumes it
--   minty  : colour picker; needs menu + volt, and `volt` is kept for <Localleader>zt
--   nvim-autopairs : NvChad enables it, but plugins/nvim-cmp.lua disables it on
--                    the full profile as buggy; keep behaviour identical here.
{{ if .exeDevVm -}}
return {
  { 'nvzone/menu', enabled = false },
  { 'nvzone/minty', enabled = false },
  { 'windwp/nvim-autopairs', enabled = false },
}
{{ else -}}
return {}
{{ end -}}
